.TH SOROKEEP 1 "2026-09-06" "sorokeep" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sorokeep - Sorokeep — The missing operations layer for deployed Soroban smart contracts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sorokeep
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sorokeep — The missing operations layer for deployed Soroban smart contracts
.SH COMMANDS
.SH WATCH
Register and start watching a contract
.SH UNWATCH
Remove a registered contract and clean up associated logs
.SH STATUS
Show TTL and storage health for watched contracts
.SH CHECK
Check TTL health for a watched contract (CI-friendly, can be forced)
.SH DAEMON
Start the monitoring daemon — polls contracts at a fixed interval
.SH ALERTS
Manage alert configurations
.SH GUARD
Configure auto-extension policy for a contract, or in bulk via --tag
.SH COSTS
Show rent costs and extension history for a contract (or the whole fleet with --fleet)
.SH RESOURCES
Show historical resource usage trends for a contract
.SH RESTORE
Restore archived entries for a contract
.SH CHANNELS
Manage channel accounts for fee bumping and transaction parallelism
.SH MCP
Start the Model Context Protocol (MCP) server on stdio transport
.SH HISTORY
Show state change history for a contract
.SH COMPLETION
Generate or query shell completion suggestions
.SH INSPECT
Inspect contract storage and token balances
.SH BUDGET
Manage monthly spending bounds for contracts
.SH DB
Backup, restore, and maintain database state
.SH PAUSE
Temporarily pause daemon polling and alerting for a contract
.SH RESUME
Resume daemon polling and alerting for a paused contract
.SH METRICS
Print a metrics snapshot without starting the HTTP server
.SH AUDIT-LOG
Export extension transactions as a machine-parseable JSONL audit trail
.SH DOCTOR
Run diagnostics for the local Sorokeep installation
.SH INIT
Interactively configure a first contract, alert channel, and guard policy
.SH CONTRACTS
List all watched contracts
.SH TAG
Manage tags on a watched contract
.SH FLEET
Show aggregate health dashboard across all watched contracts
.SH GROUP
Manage contract groups
.SH CLONE-CONFIG
Clone alert configurations and extension policies from one contract to another
.SH SEE ALSO
sorokeep(1)